* Tests: memoized shared annotation base and smaller GSEA/heatmap
  down-sampling to keep `R CMD check` within the 15-minute SPB budget.

Changes in version 0.99.16 (2026-08-08)
---------------------------------------

Bioconductor Review Round 2

* `consolidate_chromatin_loops()` now writes standard 10-column BEDPE
  (strand1/strand2 = ".") with `n_members`/`n_reps` as documented extension
  columns 11-12, making exports readable by standard tools (e.g. rtracklayer).
* `bedpe_to_gi()` tolerates header rows via explicit header tokens and
  recovers the `n_members`/`n_reps` extension columns on re-import.
* All pipeline functions return complete in-memory objects; Excel/BEDPE
  export is opt-in (`write_output = FALSE` by default).
* New internal `.require_pkg()` unifies optional-package guards; `.assert_*`
  validation family extended; `match.arg()` choices moved to signatures.
* `run_go_enrichment()` and `run_ppi_analysis()` use deterministic
  OrgDb-package-based species resolution (no fragile introspection).
* README and vignette: all demos runnable with packaged example data;
  profiling, track, and chromatin figures displayed; `reduce_ginteractions()`
  documented as a standalone utility.
* Merged reviewer PR #2 (style improvements: `anyNA`, `lengths()`, `!all()`,
  drop obsolete `getRversion` guards) and applied the same style across the
  codebase.
* Removed unused `draw_upset_intersections()` and the UpSetR hard dependency.
* Test optimisations (smaller GSEA down-sampling, fast GO unmapped-gene path,
  fixed vacuous chromatin-reclassification test); 1344 assertions passing.
* `CITATION.cff` added for GitHub homepage citation.

Changes in version 0.99.15 (2026-07-23)
-----------------------------------------

Algorithm Correctness

* Chromatin-aware target gene calling now uses a unified origin-aware
  resolver (`.resolve_chromatin_gene_role()`) that combines chromatin
  final type with anchor origin (old_type) and TSS validation.  This
  replaces the previous two-layer system where anchor-level and
  link-level role logic could diverge, and ensures consistent role
  and strict-eligibility across all output layers: map_info,
  loop_annotation, target_gene_links, and target_annotation.
* E->E (unchanged enhancer) ChIPseeker nearest genes no longer enter
  strict target columns (`Assigned_Target_Genes`, `Regulated_promoter_genes`,
  `Expanded_Target_Genes`).  They remain visible in `All_Loop_Connected_Genes`
  and `Candidate_Positional_Genes` for provenance tracking.
* E->P/dual anchors without independent TSS-supported gene mapping now
  retain `positional_candidate` role with `strict_assignment_eligible=FALSE`.
  Chromatin state is correctly recorded as promoter-like, but the
  ChIPseeker nearest gene is not promoted to a rank-1 promoter target.
  E->P/dual anchors WITH TSS-validated gene mapping are correctly
  promoted to `promoter` role with `strict_assignment_eligible=TRUE`.
* G/eG->P/dual anchors use their structural host gene (from gene-body
  overlap) as promoter-associated targets.  TSS support is not required
  for strict eligibility; when TxDb identifies an overlapping TSS gene,
  it is used as the high-confidence assignment; otherwise the host gene
  is retained with `provisional` confidence.  Evidence label changed from
  `positional_gene+promoter_like_chromatin` to
  `gene_body_host+promoter_like_chromatin`.
* New `enhancer_candidate` role (rank 3) for anchors with
  structurally-supported genes that are chromatin-downgraded to
  enhancer (P/eP/G/eG -> E).  Target priority is now:
  promoter (rank 1) > gene_body (rank 2) > enhancer_candidate (rank 3)
  > positional/fallback (rank 4).
* `.rebuild_loop_gene_summaries()` now uses `strict_assignment_eligible`
  to filter topology-expanded gene sets, preventing E-origin nearest-gene
  contamination in `Putative_Target_Genes` and `Promoter_Target_Genes`.
* `.compute_raw_promoter_stats()` now checks `anchor*_strict_eligible`
  in addition to `anchor*_gene_role`, preventing unresolved E->P/dual
  anchors from inflating promoter-centric statistics.
* `Candidate_Positional_Genes` at the loop level now aggregates all
  `strict_assignment_eligible=FALSE` gene links (including E->E
  nearest-gene candidates), not only `positional_candidate`-role links.
* Direct strict promoter–promoter co-assignment is enabled under
  `target_priority = "promoter_then_distance"`.  When path-0 and
  path-1 strict promoter links arise from two distinct anchors of
  the same direct loop and input feature, both promoter genes are
  retained in `Assigned_Target_Genes` using union semantics.
  `distance_then_role` preserves local path-first behaviour.
  `Regulated_promoter_genes` retains all eligible primary strict
  promoter links and therefore already includes both endpoints
  of a qualifying direct P–P contact.

New Evidence Labels

* `local_enhancer_candidate`, `distal_enhancer_candidate`,
  `expanded_enhancer_candidate` for enhancer-associated linkages.
* `distal_gene_body_context`, `expanded_gene_body_context` for
  gene-body linkages at path > 0.
* `expanded_positional_candidate`, `positional_candidate` for
  non-strict positional links.
* `gene_body_host+promoter_like_chromatin` for G/eG->P/dual
  host-gene evidence (replaces `positional_gene+promoter_like_chromatin`
  for G/eG-origin anchors).

Documentation

* Updated vignette reference tables for `gene_role` and `evidence`
  values to include `enhancer_candidate`, `positional_candidate`,
  and new evidence labels.
* Updated `All_Loop_Connected_Genes` Rd description to reflect
  inclusive semantics (may include enhancer and positional candidates).

Performance

* neighbor_hop = 1 no longer performs one igraph::distances() call per
  expanded anchor pair.  Because candidates are exactly 2 hops away by
  construction (2-hop ego minus direct neighbours), path_length is assigned
  directly, removing repeated graph traversals without changing results.
* Target 2-hop ego networks are now generated lazily only for anchors
  hit by the target BED, rather than for every graph node.
* First-order neighbours are cached across unique expanded anchor pairs.
* Expanded-seed anchors without gene assignments are filtered before path
  computation.  Direct-neighbour lookups use a pre-built index to avoid
  scanning the full edge table.  Identical (local, expanded) graph pairs
  are deduplicated before path computation.
* These changes affect computation only and do not alter target semantics
  or output schemas.

API

* neighbor_hop is now capped at 1.  Values >= 2 raise an error.  Direct
  1-hop loop targets are always evaluated regardless of neighbor_hop.

Algorithm Correctness

* Added `target_priority` parameter (default `"promoter_then_distance"`) to
  `annotate_peaks_and_loops()`.  The policy applies only within primary target
  links (default `path_length <= 1`); longer paths are reported separately as
  `Expanded_Target_Genes` and do not compete for `Assigned_Target_Genes`.
  `promoter_then_distance` gives promoter-linked evidence priority over
  gene-body links within the primary-link scope; `distance_then_role` restores
  the legacy path-length-dominant behaviour.  This parameter is propagated
  through expression refinement and chromatin refinement.  Tied genes with the
  same optimal priority are preserved (semicolon-delimited).
* Reordered chromatin reclassification rules to fix three blocking issues:
  (1) enhancer BED is now truly highest priority; (2) eP/eG dual_like anchors
  correctly resolve via bigWig ratio (me1_dominant → dual, unresolved → keep,
  not_me1_dominant → P); (3) eP/eG with H3K4me3+ but without H3K4me1+
  (promoter_like) revert to P.  Bivalent H3K4me3+/H3K27me3+ anchors are
  resolved by these rules (H3K4me3 defines promoter identity), not by the
  generic conflicting_marks clause.
* Triple-positive anchors (H3K4me1+/H3K4me3+/H3K27me3+) are now classified
  as conflicting_marks and retain their previous eP/eG type. Peak
  co-occurrence from bulk ChIP alone is not considered sufficient evidence
  for restoration to a functional promoter state.
* Removed duplicate E/G dual-positive rules that became unreachable after
  reordering.
* Fixed duplicate `mutate()` columns (role_rank, path_rank) that caused
  a dplyr error in `.aggregate_strict_targets()`.
* Fixed `up_meta_params` scope bug in expression refinement target finalizer.

Documentation

* Fixed BED-only mode documentation to accurately describe dual-positive anchor
  retention (H3K4me1+/H3K4me3+ anchors keep eP/eG type pending bigWig resolution).
* Removed misleading measured_set reference from reclassify_by_expression documentation.
* Corrected vignette BED-only mode descriptions for chromatin reclassification rules.
* Fixed vignette gsea_nSample default (NULL, not 99999) to match profile_target_genes().
* Fixed validate_epeG_by_chromatin() and chromatin-refine examples in vignette.
* Fixed README "within 10% of max" → "at least 10% of the group maximum" for
  co_dominance_ratio description.
* Changed "ENCODE criteria" → "ENCODE-inspired criteria" in report template (4 occurrences).

Testing & Engineering

* Removed file-level skip_on_bioc() from 3 core regression test files
  (test-regression.R, test-synthetic-invariants.R, test-review-fixes.R)
  so critical invariants run on Bioconductor builders.
* Updated 3 recompute_targets = FALSE tests to expect preserved upstream
  target tables (not NULL), matching the unified finalizer behavior.
* Added globalVariables() declarations for 30+ dplyr/data.table NSE symbols
  in annotation.R and data_processing.R, resolving R CMD check NOTES.
* Fixed roxygen block separation for .passes_expression_threshold().

Changes in version 0.99.14 (2026-06-21)
-----------------------------------------

Algorithm & Correctness

* Fixed case-sensitive gene name matching: clean_anchor() and resolve_gene_conflicts()
  now use toupper() on both sides, preventing silent P→eP misclassification when
  expression matrix row names differ in case from OrgDb SYMBOLs.
* Added biotype_order parameter to annotate_peaks_and_loops() and resolve_gene_conflicts(),
  allowing users to customise biotype priority order (e.g., prioritise lncRNAs).
* Case-insensitive diagnostic warning in expression-refinement overlap check.

Chromatin Refinement Visualizations

* Added Chromatin_Sankey: anchor-type flow diagram showing reclassification direction
  (unchanged = green, reclassified = amber).
* Added Chromatin_MarkHeatmap: aggregated ComplexHeatmap showing mark enrichment %
  per reclassification group, with N count bar annotation.
* Chromatin_Dumbbell: updated to grey-green academic palette (Original = #999999,
  Refined = #2D5A3D) for consistency with Expression Refinement module.

Documentation

* Added @seealso cross-references between annotate_peaks_and_loops(),
  refine_loop_anchors_by_expression(), refine_loop_anchors_by_chromatin(),
  and profile_target_genes().
* Updated roxygen for .build_chromatin_mark_heatmap() to match actual implementation.

Changes in version 0.99.9 (2026-05-09)
-----------------------------------------

Reviewer Response (Bisaloo, Bioconductor)

* Added package-level man page and runnable examples for all exported functions.
* Replaced sapply() with vapply(); removed <<- operator; eliminated dead code.
* Unified 0-based BED/BEDPE import and 1-based internal coordinate handling.
* Fixed GO enrichment table rendering (list-of-dataframes merge).
* Fixed expression matrix gene-name loss with single-sample-column input.
* Fixed OrgDb object handling via getFromNamespace() instead of get().
* Added whitelist-overlap cross-validation warning in expression refinement.
* Added empty-input guards for ChIPseeker::annotatePeak() and prepare_track_data().
* Replaced deprecated ggplot2 size aesthetic with linewidth.
* Improved test coverage to 84.70% with 29 dedicated regression tests.
* Updated default colour palettes to colourblind-friendly schemes (Set2, Paired, PuOr, viridis).
* looplook_report() template: enhanced metric cards, Sankey via saveWidget+iframe, aligned tables.
* Vignette: expanded comparison table, reproducibility note, BiocManager install placeholder.
* DESCRIPTION: Title case, non-package-name Description start, removed recursive SystemRequirements, expanded Suggests.
* Precomputed results now accepted as in-memory list or file path; bedpe_file optional.

